# disabled.xosv - a service that is present but not started.
#
# `start` is absent, so the supervisor reads this, finds no instruction to run it, and
# moves on. That is the point: a service can sit on disk turned off without
# being deleted, and turning it on is adding one line rather than remembering
# what the file used to contain.
#
# It also proves the walk finds more than one descriptor, which the single
# staged service could not.

exec=/System/Programs/hi.xcex
args=this should never print
grants=console
